# Conformance probe pack for `when` ranges and lists on a sequential layout
# and for a `switch` inside a kind on a common key (spec 0.20), most
# significant bit first. Public.
#
#   x : 8, common
#   kind a   when 8 0..9          y : 8, then switch x: 1 z : 8, else nothing
#   kind b   when 8 12..14,10     w : 8      encode writes 12, the lo of the
#                                            range listed first
format     conformance-kinds-seq
version    0.20.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field  probe.x  8  uint
kind   a
when   8  0..9
requires probe.y
field  probe.y  8  uint
switch probe.x
  case 1
    field  probe.z  8  uint
  else
end
kind   b
when   8  12..14,10
requires probe.w
field  probe.w  8  uint
